WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:08.540
So this really has to be seen to be believed,
FOX host Lou Dobbs has been one of the major

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.270
nodes of spreading bogus election fraud claims
since November 3rd.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:19.380
He's done everything from interview that wacky
lawyer, Sydney Powell, to interviewing supposed

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.510
witnesses of voter fraud who signed affidavits.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:29.340
He's been full on with this thing, repeating
and allowing the promotion of completely baseless

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.210
claims about companies like Dominion Voting
and Smartmatic and others.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.449
He's really been full on with this thing.

00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:41.449
And then suddenly, a couple of days ago, Lou
Dobbs aired a fact check that debunked his

00:00:41.449 --> 00:00:44.010
own election conspiracy theories.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.639
What on earth is going on and what's going
on is fascinating.

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:51.479
It turns out that Smartmatic, which is one
of the companies that makes voting machines

00:00:51.479 --> 00:00:56.179
about which Lou Dobbs has been spreading this
information, Smartmatic wrote a legal demand

00:00:56.179 --> 00:01:02.549
letter to Fox News, Newsmax and on threatening
legal action if they don't retract their completely

00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:04.920
bogus claims about Smartmatic.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.100
And the letter actually quotes Lou Dobbs.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:14.750
It quotes Fox host Maria Bartiromo and others
who simply will not stop making insane claims

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.390
about voter fraud.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:22.299
And it looks like Fox lawyers decided that
the letters had some teeth because Lou Dobbs

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:28.310
ended up airing the following segment, which
please understand this key part.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:35.439
This segment debunks the lies Lou himself
was telling over the last five weeks.

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:40.400
And Lou just looks absolutely miserable introducing
this segment.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:46.030
And what's fascinating is that this is clearly
a pre produced segment meant specifically

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.969
to get Fox News out of legal hot water.

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:53.469
The questions are asked in voiceover They're
all very carefully worded.

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:54.820
It's stunning to watch this.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:55.820
Take a look.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.149
Lots of opinions about the integrity of the
election, the irregularities of mail in voting

00:02:01.149 --> 00:02:04.490
of election voting machines and voting software.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.829
One of the companies is Smartmatic.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:12.100
And we reached out to one of the leading authorities
on open source software for elections, Eddie

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.830
Perez, for his insight and views.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:21.670
Eddie is the global director of tech development
at the Open Source Election Technology Institute.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:28.680
We ask him for his assessment of Smartmatic
and recent claims about the company.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:33.050
Have you seen any evidence that Smartmatic
software was used to flip votes anywhere in

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.480
the U.S. in this election?

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:42.920
I have not seen any evidence that Smartmatic
software was used to delete, change, alter

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.980
anything related to vote tabulation.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.480
Smartmatic says its software was never used
outside of L.A. County in twenty twenty.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.610
Do you know whether or not that's true?

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:52.880
That is my understanding.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:03:00.630
Smartmatic functioned as the contract manufacturer
for the Los Angeles County voting system,

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:05.450
and that was a customized system that was
effectively built to the county's order.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:10.580
I am not aware of them having any other direct
customers relationships with election officials

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.870
in the United States.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.570
What about Smartmatic and Dominion?

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.880
Do you know if they're related, whether one
owns the other, whether Dominion uses Smartmatic

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.880
software?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:24.960
Both Dominion and Smartmatic have individually
and respectively put out very clear statements

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.460
from their corporate headquarters, each of
them indicating they are independent companies.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.660
They are not related to each other.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.390
It is my understanding that neither one of
them has an ownership stake in the other or

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.780
anything like that.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:46.600
So that directly debunks the things that Lou
Dobbs and his guests have been claiming, including

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:52.480
as an example that there's some kind of nefarious
link between Smartmatic and Dominion voting

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.480
systems.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.950
And then at the end of the segment, they just
cut directly to commercial.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.810
No explanation, no commentary from Lou Dobbs.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:01.830
Totally abrupt.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:02.830
Take a look.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:07.710
And this is right after debunking another
one of Lou Dobbs previous claims says in which

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:12.870
Smartmatic technology was banned in the U.S.
in 2020 due to security weaknesses or wrongdoing.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:19.640
I am not I'm not aware of any instances where
smart mattocks technology was banned in the

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:20.640
US.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.130
Again, it is my understanding that outside
of one customer in Los Angeles County, Smartmatic

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.970
has no presence in the voting technology marketplace
in the United States.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:40.180
Heading into retirement, right to commercial
with with no word from Lou Dobbs there about

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.680
how he has been making the opposite claims
